Dear Ogi,

Our conversations about "paying kindness forward" have stayed with me. It is a beautiful philosophy, and it has inspired the way I want to approach the meditation center.

I am deeply touched by your offer to let me build on your land. It is a gesture of trust that I value immensely. Because I view this center not as a financial asset, but as a mission of trust and a legacy for my godchild, (Mimi is pregnant and I have been asked to be godparent), I want to ensure that this project is a blessing to both of us, and to all of our families, for decades to come.

As a businessman, you know that the best way to protect a friendship is to have total clarity. Therefore, I have outlined a proposal that allows us to keep the "heart" of the project while ensuring the "structure" is sound.

The Vision
I intend to build a modest, high-quality meditation center (approx. 90m²) and a surrounding garden. It will be a place of silence and healing, designed to blend into the beauty of your land. If possible I would like to buy a agricultural adjacent plot that makes the center more selfsufficient and is a good investment for me :)

The Framework of Trust
To ensure this project remains a gift and not a burden, I propose the following:

Ownership & Investment: I will provide 100% of the funding for the design, construction, and lifelong maintenance of the center. The land remains yours, and I will respect it as such.
The Legacy: My intention is to build this as a sanctuary that I can eventually gift to my godchild. I would like us to agree on a long-term right of use that allows the center to transition to them in the future.
Zero Burden: To keep our friendship clean and simple, the center will be entirely independent. I will arrange for its own utility connections (water/electricity) and cover all associated taxes and upkeep. You will not have to contribute a single lev or hour of labor.
The Safety Valve: I want you to feel completely secure. If the center is ever abandoned or the legacy ends, the buildings and improvements will revert to your ownership.

The Path Forward
I don't want this to be a cold transaction, but a shared project of kindness. I suggest we meet soon to discuss:

The exact location on your 8 hectares that would be most harmonious.
A simple legal agreement that protects your ownership while securing the center’s future.

Thank you for your kindness and for helping me turn this vision into a reality. I look forward to building this sanctuary with your blessing.

With gratitude and respect,

Hjalmar
